{
  "name": "ChatApp — Daily Digest (n8n)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Setup (do this once before activating)\n\n1. **Config node** (below): edit `baseUrl` to your ChatApp.Api URL (e.g. `https://your-backend.example.com`, no trailing slash), and `onBehalfOfUsername` to the username of an existing **Administrator**-role account (§4.2 — role-based auth: every backend call below now sends `X-On-Behalf-Of` with this username, not just the service key).\n2. **Credential — \"ChatApp N8n Key\"**: create an *HTTP Header Auth* credential named exactly `ChatApp N8n Key`, header name `X-Client-Key`, value = the `Clients:N8nKey` secret the backend owner gives you. Every HTTP Request node below already references it by name — open each once and pick it from the credential dropdown if it shows as unlinked after import.\n3. **Google Sheets node** (\"Append To Google Sheet\"): open it, connect your own Google Sheets credential, and pick/create a spreadsheet + sheet with header row: `Type | ConversationId | DisplayName | Summary | GeneratedAt`.\n4. **Schedule Trigger**: change the time if you don't want the default (daily at 00:00).\n5. **Webhook (bottom-left)**: this is the \"web page\" — see the design note near it. If n8n is self-hosted with no public URL, use n8n's built-in tunnel or a reverse proxy so the webhook URL is reachable.\n\nReference docs this workflow was built from: `mcp-n8n-api-reference.md` (auth model, DTOs, endpoint table) + `openapi.json` (exact request shapes).",
        "height": 332,
        "width": 1140
      },
      "id": "200cfa35-c750-41d9-9cb0-02979cf97e5e",
      "name": "Setup — read me first",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -608,
        -144
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Why a Webhook node is \"the web page\"\n\n`mcp-n8n-api-reference.md` §6 is explicit: `POST /api/internal/digest` only **broadcasts** the digest (SignalR `DigestPublished`) — the backend does **not** store or serve it back. The workflow itself must own publishing/persisting it somewhere viewable.\n\nThis workflow uses n8n's own **Webhook (GET) + workflow static data** as that \"somewhere\" — zero extra hosting, zero extra signups. The Schedule branch stores the latest digest HTML via `$getWorkflowStaticData('global')`; the Webhook branch reads it back and renders it. The Webhook's public URL *is* the web page.\n\n**Alternative** if you need a persistent URL independent of this n8n instance's uptime: swap the last 3 nodes for a GitHub node committing `digest.html` to a GitHub Pages repo, or an HTTP Request to any static-file host. Not done here to avoid an extra credential for a take-home.",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 740
      },
      "id": "152f063d-9408-412a-bfef-c9e1734b11c6",
      "name": "Design note — the web page",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1760,
        944
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## If a Merge node's mode looks wrong after import\n\nn8n occasionally renames Merge-node dropdown options between versions.\n\n- **Merge Branches** should combine **1 item + 1 item by position** into one item (per-thread summaries + the 24h roll-up).\n- **Merge For Sheet** should just **append/concatenate** two lists of items into one longer list (thread rows + the overall row).\n\nIf either shows a different mode after import, open the node and pick the option matching the description above — the rest of the workflow doesn't care how the mode is labeled, only that the *result* matches.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 380
      },
      "id": "edb4e055-7562-49f3-84c7-a322a7485379",
      "name": "Merge node note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1040,
        1280
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## One thread's AI failure must not break the whole digest\n\n\"Summarize Thread\" and \"Get 24h Rollup\" both have **Continue On Fail** enabled. If Gemini hiccups for one conversation (rate limit, timeout), the next Code node substitutes a placeholder string instead of the run aborting — mirroring the backend's own \"AI failure never blocks\" rule (F-5) at the workflow level.\n\nThis also absorbs a real access-control gap: `POST /api/conversations/{id}/summary` only allows a caller who is a **participant** of that conversation. `GET /api/internal/conversations` lists every conversation, regardless of membership. If the `onBehalfOfUsername` Administrator is not a participant of some thread, that thread's summary call gets 403 and falls back to the placeholder — not a bug, just something to know if placeholders show up often.",
        "height": 156,
        "width": 716
      },
      "id": "11fa5780-e3a6-4c12-80b5-800c258c94b8",
      "name": "Resilience note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -864,
        624
      ]
    },
